  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n8{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2033}+5x(x+2){y}^{\u2032}-3y=0\n$$\n\nLet $y={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a Frobenius series solution about the regular singular point $x=0$ of the differential equation above.\nFind $f(n),$ given that $\\lambda \\in (0,\\frac{3}{5})$ and the recurrence relation for ${a}_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{5(1-2n)}{f(n)}\\,{a}_{n-1},\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$\n\n*Hint: Substituting the Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2033} & =8({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ 5x(x+2){y}^{\u2032} & =10\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[5(\\lambda +n-1){a}_{n-1}+10(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}]{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ -3y & =-3{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }3{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*",
